<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Telecom down 4.93 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Telecom down 4.93 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan Telecommunication Company Ltd (PTCL) tumbled 1.65 rupees, or 4.93 percent, to 31.85 on Tuesday, falling victim to general bearish sentiment, dealers said.</p>
<p>About 1.63 million PTCL shares had changed hands by noon.</p>
<p>&quot;General market sentiment is very bad,&quot; dealer Manochar Jamal said. &quot;Confidence has been eroded by continued political uncertainty and bleak economic prospects.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;Most blue chips are down on short-selling as people expect prices to fall further,&quot; dealer Hina Akhlaq said.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192.</p>
